# Radical Complexity

**Authors:** Jean-Philippe Bouchaud

## Summary
This is an informal and sketchy review of six topical, somewhat unrelated subjects in quantitative finance: rough volatility models; random covariance matrix theory; copulas; crowded trades; high-frequency trading &amp; market stability; and "radical complexity" &amp; scenario based (macro)economics. Some open questions and research directions are briefly discussed.


